        "id": 1106949
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-05-20T20:25:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think we should assume all types may have multiple chips.\n\nI also think we should make i2c_lookup more generic. As Julius also pointed out, i2c_lookup has to deal with PD port numbers (instead of I2C port numbers) because if chips are in a hybrid bus topology, Depthcharge needs to know which [i2c_port, i2c_addr] belongs to which PD chip.\n\nSince i2c_lookup has to deal with PD port numbers, we should convert it to a generic lookup command returning bus type:\n\n\t#define EC_CMD_BUS_LOOKUP\n\tstruct ec_response_bus_lookup {\n\t\tuint8_t bus_type;  /* EC_BUS_TYPE_I2C, _SPI, ... */\n\t\tunion {\n\t\t\tstruct ec_i2c_info;\n\t\t\tstruct ec_spi_info;\n\t\t\t...\n\t\t}\n\t} __ec_align2;",
      "parentUuid": "7ce519e2_9cfe0792",
